# Node / Vite
node_modules/
viewer/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Icons live once in data/_assets/icons and are mirrored into the viewer at
# build time by viewer/scripts/copy-icons.mjs (wired to predev/prebuild).
viewer/public/icons/

# Scraper HTTP cache — large, regenerable, never worth committing
data/_cache/
data/_logs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*

# Generated analysis reports. `recommend --all` rewrites one per god (89 of
# them) and `validate` / `analysis` / the scheduled refresh rewrite the rest,
# so any model change lands ~94 files of regenerated prose on top of the few
# files that actually decided anything. The 2026-08-19 effect-tag pass was 317
# files, of which ten held the change.
#
# NOT the whole directory. `data/Analysis/snapshots/` is an INPUT, not a
# report — `build_index` reads it for the viewer's patch notes — so it stays
# tracked, and the `*.md` pattern leaves it alone.
data/Analysis/*.md
# `_calibration.md` is the exception that earns its place: it is the
# leakage-free gate's own output, it is byte-for-byte deterministic (verified
# 2026-08-19 by running it twice), and it therefore changes ONLY when the model
# does. That makes its diff the single clearest record of what a commit did to
# the gate. Drop this line if you would rather regenerate it to find out.
!data/Analysis/_calibration.md
